## While Loop
Sometimes, you want repeated work, and writing the same code over . . . and over . . . and over . . . is _very_ bad, because let's say you want to make a change and forget somewhere? That is what loops are: they just repeat work. A `while` loop runs as long as its condition is true:
```csharp
int i = 0;
while (i < 5) {
    Console.WriteLine(i);
    i++;
}
```

